00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:54.809
Is it good for you?

00:01:54.809 --> 00:01:56.377
Probably not.

00:01:56.377 --> 00:02:00.020
#1 Aspartame is a lot more
sweet than regular sugar

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.957
and it conditions your
brain to want more sugar.

00:02:02.957 --> 00:02:04.688
#2 There exists bacteria in your gut.

00:02:04.688 --> 00:02:07.350
That bacteria loves sugar.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.760
And that's the unhealthy
bacteria that loves the sugar.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.300
You don't want those bacteria around

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.280
because they cause you to gain weight.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.309
They actually influence your
cravings to want more food.

00:02:16.309 --> 00:02:19.060
And when you eat aspartame,
you don't digest it,

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.540
so you don't get the calories and sugar

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.340
but the bacteria do.
- Whoa!

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:25.340
- So you increase the number
of bacteria that craves sugars

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.820
so you're going to want more sugar.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.500
That bacteria makes you
more likely to eat more food

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.330
and get obese and all these things.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.880
If you want something sweet occasionally,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.320
